Dear mentors,

I am looking for review and an upload sponsor for my package
qsm-pve-direct, initially targeting experimental/contrib:

* Package name    : qsm-pve-direct
  Version         : 0.4.0+20261020-1~exp1
  Upstream author : Dmitry R <rdmitry0911@gmail.com>
* URL             : https://github.com/rdmitry0911/qsm-rd
* License         : GPL-3.0-or-later, AGPL-3.0-or-later, MIT/X11
* Section         : contrib/net
* ITP             : https://bugs.debian.org/1151422

QSM streams QEMU D-Bus displays and optional LXC desktops to a browser
using WebRTC, with software or optional hardware video encoding, audio
and interactive input. Existing PVE authentication and permissions gate
console access. The standalone implementation uses official Proxmox
packages; pve-manager and qemu-server remain external runtime dependencies,
which is why I propose contrib. Build dependencies are in Debian main.

The source review release, signatures and validation are available at:
https://github.com/rdmitry0911/qsm-rd/releases/tag/v0.4.0-debian-contrib-20261020-review1

Download the source with:
dget -x https://github.com/rdmitry0911/qsm-rd/releases/download/v0.4.0-debian-contrib-20261020-review1/qsm-pve-direct_0.4.0+20261020-1~exp1.dsc

The release includes the project signing certificate. Primary fingerprint:
BA99528182B7EADD0199B6986A09741B1DBEAEF2
These are project release signatures, not Debian Developer signatures.

The package uses debhelper, generated shared-library dependencies, normal
source packaging and hardening flags. It builds the LXC guest deb from
the same source before embedding it in the optional host helper; no
prebuilt release deb or network download is used during the build.

Validation includes unprivileged builds with networking disabled on
Debian 13 and current unstable, 19 passing CTest tests, clean Lintian
source/binary checks, and a passing source-units autopkgtest on unstable.
The upstream standalone release has separate browser/PVE runtime tests.
The new debhelper maintainer-script integration still needs PVE lifecycle
review; these clean-build checks are not a claim that a new Debian upload
has been qualified on production PVE hosts. I would appreciate that review
before an experimental upload.

Project development is sponsored by Takt: https://taktcycles.com/
Takt is the project sponsor; I am seeking a Debian Developer upload sponsor.
The implementation and packaging use AI assistance, disclosed in the source
and ITP. I intend to maintain the package and respond to review and bug reports.

Changelog:
  * Initial contrib packaging preview for review. (Closes: #1151422)
  * Build the media worker and host/guest profiles from source with debhelper.
  * Retain the external Proxmox runtime dependencies explicitly.

